:: AskAboutPlants [childhood]
# Nature's Pantry

"Which plants can we eat?" you ask, pointing to various items your mother has gathered.

She smiles at your curiosity and pulls out several different berries and seeds from her pouch. With patience, she shows you the differences between edible and poisonous varieties.

"These red berries with the star pattern on the bottom are sweet and good to eat," she explains. "But these," she points to similar-looking berries with a slightly different shape, "will make your stomach hurt terribly."

She teaches you to look at leaf shapes, berry colors, and growth patterns. "The forest provides everything we need, but we must know how to read its signs."

You learn that some plants are food in one season but not in another, and that certain parts of a plant might be edible while others are harmful.

"Always ask an adult before eating any plant you find," she warns. "Until you are certain, it is better to be safe."

